# Every text file in this repo is LF in git, always.
#
# Why this file exists: on 2026-09-16 nineteen files came back from an
# editing pass with CRLF line endings. The content was byte-identical
# after stripping the CRs, but git saw nineteen fully rewritten files, so
# the diff for that day's work was unreadable -- and one of them was
# 031_opening_balance.sql, a migration that had already been applied to
# production. src/db/migrate.js checksums each migration file's bytes
# (checksumOf, sha256 of the file) and compares it with the checksum
# recorded in schema_migrations, so flipping LF to CRLF makes an applied
# migration look edited on every subsequent run. That warning would have
# been correct and useless at the same time: nothing about the SQL had
# changed.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` means git normalises to LF on commit and checks out
# LF on every platform, Windows included. Node, Postgres and every tool in
# this repo read LF fine on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touched, never normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
